  "name": "Propose a better Qodo configuration after a merge",
  "notes": "Steps: fetch and reset the dedicated checkout to origin/main (machine.command on qodo-checkout); http.call POST /runs on associate-bridge with the checkout, model, test commands and the instruction (the instruction lives only here); a retry_until loop of pause (30 s), GET /runs/{id} and a status line, until the status is no longer running (40 polls, about 20 minutes, a clear loop_max_exceeded otherwise); a one-pass check that fails the run unless the status is finished and ok is true (lost, failed-to-start and a failed or unmerged run fail here with the run's own words); when merge is merged, http.call POST /verbs/config/propose on qodo-bridge with base = the run's base_commit (nothing_to_merge ends the run quietly, succeeded, with no PR); a one-pass check that fails the run with the refusal's reason and detail when the bridge refuses; then github.pr_open on github-app with the returned files, the fixed branch qodo-config/update and the labels qodo-config, automated. A configuration PR still open makes the next run end with skipped: branch_exists (the one-open-PR rule), succeeded.",
  "outputs": [
    {
      "name": "run",
      "source": "steps.run.outputs.value",
      "type": "object"
    },
    {
      "name": "pr_number",
      "source": "steps.open_pr.outputs.number",
      "type": "integer"
    },
